{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[],"authorship_tag":"ABX9TyOQunYnNNuzKwfOGlsecwbq"},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Implementation of **K-Means** and **K-Medoid**"],"metadata":{"id":"lpAg84pk2rz1"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Aim**-To implement K means and K medoid using python and plot the scatter plot for the output\n","\n","**Theory**-\n","\n","**K means Clustering**:-\n","\n","  K means is a centroid based clistering algorithm.\n","\n","   For a given value of K,the algorithm:\n","  1. Select K initial centroid.\n","  2. Assign each data point to its nearest centroid.\n","  3. Calculate the new cetroid of each cluster.\n","  4. Reassigns the points based on the new centroids.\n","  5. Repeats the process untill the centroids become stable\n","  The centroid is calculated using the mean of all points in the cluster.\n","\n","\n","**K Medoid Clustering**:-\n","\n"," K-Medoid is similar to K-Mean,but unstead of using the mean as the cluster center,it selects an actual data points from the datset as cluster center.THis point is called medoid.THe algorithm attempts to select medoids such that the total distance between the data points and their assigned medoids in minimized.\n","\n","K-Medoids is generally more robust to outlires thatn K-Means"],"metadata":{"id":"QR6QEyOj4Y_c"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# KMean Clustering"],"metadata":{"id":"Z7O4MIe51ef9"}},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"id":"8911baa0","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":466},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1793951470366,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":3968,"user":{"displayName":"24CSEAIML256 KORADA SRAVANTH KUMAR","userId":"04889142993122972578"}},"outputId":"88e8f41a-5e40-41a9-c2be-2919ab8ff9a4"},"source":["# K Means Clustering\n","\n","import numpy as np\n","from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","# Create dataset\n","X = np.array([\n","    [2, 3],\n","    [3, 5],\n","    [4, 4],\n","    [8, 7],\n","    [9, 9],\n","    [10, 8]\n","])\n","\n","# Apply K-Means clustering\n","Kmeans = KMeans(n_clusters=2, random_state=0, n_init=10)\n","Kmeans.fit(X)\n","\n","# Get labels and cluster centers\n","labels = Kmeans.labels_\n","centers = Kmeans.cluster_centers_\n","\n","# Print cluster centers\n","print(Kmeans.cluster_centers_)\n","\n","# Plot the clusters\n","plt.scatter(X[:, 0], X[:, 1], c=Kmeans.labels_)\n","\n","# Plot cluster centers\n","plt.scatter(\n","    Kmeans.cluster_centers_[:, 0],\n","    Kmeans.cluster_centers_[:, 1],\n","    c='red',\n","    marker='X',\n","    s=200\n",")\n","\n","plt.show()"],"execution_count":1,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["[[9. 8.]\n"," [3. 4.]]\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# K Medoid Clustering"],"metadata":{"id":"N2f7ZQUC1YJF"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["!pip install scikit-learn-extra\n","\n","import numpy as np\n","from sklearn_extra.cluster import KMedoids\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","# Create dataset\n","X = np.array([\n","    [2, 3],\n","    [3, 5],\n","    [4, 4],\n","    [8, 7],\n","    [9, 9],\n","    [10, 8]\n","])\n","\n","# Apply K-Medoids clustering\n","Kmedoids = KMedoids(n_clusters=2, random_state=0)\n","Kmedoids.fit(X)\n","\n","# Get labels and cluster centers\n","labels = Kmedoids.labels_\n","centers = Kmedoids.cluster_centers_\n","\n","# Print cluster centers\n","print(Kmedoids.cluster_centers_)\n","\n","# Plot the clusters\n","plt.scatter(X[:, 0], X[:, 1], c=Kmedoids.labels_)\n","\n","# Plot medoid centers\n","plt.scatter(\n","    Kmedoids.cluster_centers_[:, 0],\n","    Kmedoids.cluster_centers_[:, 1],\n","    c='red',\n","    marker='X',\n","    s=200\n",")\n","\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_u